Z||000013||DecadenceR||06-06-2001||03:41 PM||||Originally i never knew what a Fiero was.<BR>I remember back in 89-90, I was throwing out some old magazines, and I found an ad for the Toyota MR2. I thought it was the sweetest car... And this from a die-hard Camaro boy.<BR>But when I finally realized the Fiero... No contest!!! I had a guy at Sam's Club, where I used to run the tire shop, come in with an MR2. I asked him about it and showed him my old 87 Fiero coupe. He almost MADE me take his car out to see how I liked it compared the Fiero (he owned a garaged 88GT). I liked a few interior differences, but the Fiero had the MR2 HANDS down. No contest.<P>Anyway, from what I've noticed of the young girls, HS girls, is that if the car looks good, runs nice, and has a good system, it can be anything. They don't care. They just want to be seen in it by their friends. And no offense to any of the WOMEN in here. But little girls are just that. And I know this from past experience.  ;-)||||reg||1
Z||000014||FieroHeather||06-06-2001||11:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DecadenceR:<BR><B>Anyway, from what I've noticed of the young girls, HS girls, is that if the car looks good, runs nice, and has a good system, it can be anything. They don't care. They just want to be seen in it by their friends. And no offense to any of the WOMEN in here. But little girls are just that. And I know this from past experience.  ;-)</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>From a female perspective, a nice car equals a guy who has future potential.  Owning a car shows responsibility, financial steadyness (or attempting financial stability) and the ability to get somewhere away from the parental units.  In High School, I personally did not make owning a car a priority for a potential boyfriend.  But when I was in College, a guy with a car was much higher on the list as a potential boyfriend than was a guy who only used the bus to get around town.  <P>Have I mentioned that it was the Fiero that enhanced my relationship with my current bf?  When I saw that sweet car, I *knew* that there was future potential with him.  I knew that I was dating someone who was going to make something good of his life.  I cannot wait to marry that dude  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  And no, I probably even then will not get to drive it!  IMO, Fieros are a great investment, both socially, and in entertainment value.||||reg||7
Z||000015||DecadenceR||06-06-2001||11:22 PM||||Not to dispute you, but from my experience, and again this is just from people I know, it's more of a popularity contest. "My boyfriends car looks phat" "Well MY boyfriends' car has the baset system" and so on.<BR>HOwever, I do see your point. But like you said, I think that's more of an older "womanhood" thing than a "girl" thing. Did I make any sense?||||reg||1
