Z||000020||DecadenceR||06-07-2001||09:39 AM||||Yeah, what the hell!!!<BR>This girl that lives in my development came up to me the other day and just started talking to me because she liked my hair (it's dyed bright red) and let me tell you, this girl was GORGEOUS!!! <BR>I asked her how old she was, and she's like "I'm gonna be 15 in a few weeks..."<BR>I was like Okay, I think your mom is calling you to change your diaper...<BR>When i was 15, girls look like 8 year olds do today. How come we all missed out on this????<P>Anyway, I took a friend of a friend for a ride in my car the other day. She got in, turned around, and was like "you only have 2 seats???"<BR>I told her no, there are 2 more but I folded them up because i don't need them, since I personally use one at a time.||||reg||1
Z||000021||Ken Wittlief||06-07-2001||10:41 AM||||okay - all the joking aside, the thing that impresses most HS girls the most is if your car is clean and sparkly, and the wheels are shiny at night, the interior is spotless, and she feels like a princess riding around in your car.<P>  Open sunroof is a big plus!<P>  the other thing to keep in mind, babes like guys who are stong, but gentle. So when you are riding around with a babe in your car, make sure you are not snapping her head back and forth everytime you shift or brake. Keep that horsepower in reserve, us it sparingly, and then she will be thrilled when you ocasionally squish her back into the passenger seat with your right foot. Overdo it and she will think you drive like an idiot - usually once is enough, so she knows the car has got 'IT' when you want it.<P>  maybe the fact that you have taken a 15 year old 'sad song and made it better' and you stick it out and have a loyality thing showing there, might score some points - a long term commitment, even if it is to a car.<P>   what you dont want them to think is your car is more important then THEY are - if they get the impression you spend 30 hrs a week in your garage fawning over your wheels, then when will you have time to lavish attention on them?<P>   In a subtle way your car will reveal something about your character to them - which can be a good thing.<P>   BTW, if they like Mustangs, then "No, this is not a mustang - but Mustangs are sooooo cool....." Most girls do not have a very deep understanding of cars and whats under the hood, so if they get it in their head, for whatever reason, that mustangs are awesome, and you start explaining to them how stupid they are for thinking that way, you may be right<P>   but you will be driving home alone.<P>   #1 rule for babes - never make them feel stupid - even if they are wrong keep your mouth shut and change the subject.||||reg||1
